{
  "title": "58: al-Mujaadelah المجادلة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nقَدْ سَمِعَ اللّٰهُ قَوْلَ الَّتِىْ تُجَادِلُكَ فِىْ زَوْجِهَا وَ تَشْتَكِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ ۖ وَاللّٰهُ يَسْمَعُ تَحَاوُرَكُمَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ ۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(1)\nQAD SAMEA’A LAAHO QAWLA LATEE TUJAADELUKA FEE ZAWJEHAA WA TASHTAKEAA ELAL LAAHE WAL LAAHO YASMA-O’ TAHAAWURAKUMAA INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N BASEER.\nAllah has indeed heard (and accepted) the statement of the woman who pleads with thee concerning her husband and carries her complaint (in prayer) to Allah: and Allah (always) hears the arguments between both sides among you: for Allah hears and sees (all things). \nاَلَّذِيْنَ يُظٰهِرُوْنَ مِنْكُمْ مِّنْ نِّسَآئِهِمْ مَّا هُنَّ اُمَّهٰتِهِمْؕ اِنْ اُمَّهٰتُهُمْ اِلَّا الّٰٓىِئْ وَلَدْنَهُمْؕ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مُنْكَرًا مِّنَ الْقَوْلِ وَزُوْرًاؕ وَ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُوْرٌ‏(2)\nLAZEENA YUZAAHEROONA MINKUM MIN NESAAA-EHIM MAA HUNNA AUMMAHAATEHEM IN AUMMAHAATUHUM ILLAL ALLAAA WALADNAHUM WA INNAHUM LAYAQOOLOONA MUNKARAN MENAL AL-QAWLE WAZOORAN WA INNAL LAAHA LAA’AFOO GHAFOORUR.\nIf any men among you divorce their wives by Zihar (calling them mothers), they cannot be their mothers: None can be their mothers except those who gave them birth. And in fact they use words (both) iniquitous and false: but truly Allah is one that blots out (sins), and forgives (again and again). \nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُظٰهِرُوْنَ مِنْ نِّسَآئِهِمْ ثُمَّ يَعُوْدُوْنَ لِمَا قَالُوْا فَتَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّتَمَآسَّا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ تُوْعَظُوْنَ بِهٖ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(3)\nWAL LAZEENA YUZAAHEROONA MIN NESAAA-EHIM SUMMA YAU’OODOONA LEMAKH QAALOO FATAHREERU RAQABATIN MIN QABLE AN YYATAMAASSAA ZAA ZAALEKUM TOOA’AZOONA BEHI WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nBut those who divorce their wives by Zihar, then wish to go back on the words they uttered, (It is ordained that such a one) should free a slave before they touch each other: Thus are ye admonished to perform: and Allah is well-acquainted with (all) that ye do. \nفَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّتَمَآسَّاؕ فَمَنْ لَّمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَاِطْعَامُ سِتِّيْنَ مِسْكِيْنًاؕ ذٰلِكَ لِتُؤْمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَتِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِؕ وَلِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابٌ اَلِیْمٌ‏(4)\nFAMAN LAM YAJID FA-SEYAAMO SHAHRAYNE MUTATAABEA’AYNE MIN QABLE AN YYATAMAASSAA FAMAN LAM YASTATEA’ FAATA’AAMU SETTEENA MESKEENAN ZAALEKA LE-LAM TOAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WARASOOLEH WA TILKAL TILKA LAAH WA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nAnd if any has not (the wherewithal), he should fast for two months consecutively before they touch each other. But if any is unable to do so, he should feed sixty indigent ones, this, that ye may show your faith in Allah and His Messenger. Those are limits (set by) Allah. For those who reject (Him), there is a grievous Penalty. \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُحَآدُّوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ كُبِتُوْا كَمَا كُبِتَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ وَقَدْ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍ ؕ وَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ ۚ‏(5)\nINNAL LAZEENA YUHAADDOONA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU KUBETOOA KAMAA KUBETA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WA QAD ANZALNAA AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT WA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nThose who resist Allah and His Messenger will be humbled to dust, as were those before them: for We have already sent down Clear Signs. And the Unbelievers (will have) a humiliating Penalty, \nيَوْمَ يَبْعَثُهُمُ اللّٰهُ جَمِيْعًا فَيُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا ؕ اَحْصٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ وَنَسُوْهُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(6)\nYAWMA YABA’ASUHUMU LAAHO JAMEE-A’A FAYUNABBEUHUM BEMAA A’MELOO AAHSAAHU LAAHO WANASOOHU WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WA.\nOn the Day that Allah will raise them all up (again) and show them the Truth (and meaning) of their conduct. Allah has reckoned its (value), though they may have forgotten it, for Allah is Witness to all things. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ مَا يَكُوْنُ مِنْ نَّجْوٰى ثَلٰثَةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ رَابِعُهُمْ وَلَا خَمْسَةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ سَادِسُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَدْنٰى مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ وَلَاۤ اَكْثَرَ اِلَّا هُوَ مَعَهُمْ اَيْنَ مَا كَانُوْاۚ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(7)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ MAA LAHUL MIN NNAJWAA SALAASATIN ILLAA HOWA RAABEU’UHUM WA LAA KHAMSATIN ILLAA HOWA SAADESUHUM WA LAA ADNAA MIN ZAA LEKA WA LAA AKSARAN ILLAA HOWA MA-A’HUM AYNA MAA KAANOO SUMMA YUNABBEUHUM BEMAA A’MELOO YAWMA QEYAAMATE INNAL LAAHA BEKULLE SHAYIN A’LEEM.\nSeest thou not that Allah doth know (all) that is in the heavens and on earth? There is not a secret consultation between three, but He makes the fourth among them, - Nor between five but He makes the sixth, nor between fewer nor more, but He is in their midst, wheresoever they be: In the end will He tell them the truth of their conduct, on the Day of Judgment. For Allah has full knowledge of all things. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ نُهُوْا عَنِ النَّجْوٰى ثُمَّ يَعُوْدُوْنَ لِمَا نُهُوْا عَنْهُ وَيَتَنٰجَوْنَ بِالْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَمَعْصِيَتِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَاِذَا جَآءُوْكَ حَيَّوْكَ بِمَا لَمْ يُحَيِّكَ بِهِ اللّٰهُۙ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ لَوْلَا يُعَذِّبُنَا اللّٰهُ بِمَا نَقُوْلُؕ حَسْبُهُمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ يَصْلَوْنَهَاۚ فَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(8)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA NUHOOA A’NIL AN-NAJWAA SUMMA YAU’OODOONA LEMAKH NUHOOA A’NHO WAYATANAAJAWNA BIL-ISME WAL U’UDWAANE WAMAA’SEETE RASOOLE WA EZAA JAAOOKA HAYWKA BEMAA LAM YUHAYKA BEHIL LAAHO WA YAQOOLOONA FEE ANFOSEHIM LAWLAA YUA’AZZEBUNAA LAAHO BEMAA NAQOOLU HASBUHUM JAHANNAMUL YASLAWNAHAA FA MASALUL MASEER.\nTurnest thou not thy sight towards those who were forbidden secret counsels yet revert to that which they were forbidden (to do)? And they hold secret counsels among themselves for iniquity and hostility, and disobedience to the Messenger. And when they come to thee, they salute thee, not as Allah salutes thee, (but in crooked ways): And they say to themselves, “Why does not Allah punish us for our words?” Enough for them is Hell: In it will they burn, and evil is that destination! \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا تَنَاجَيْتُمْ فَلَا تَتَنَاجَوْا بِالْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَمَعْصِيَتِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَتَنَاجَوْا بِالْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوٰىؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(9)\nYAA-AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA TANAAJAYTUM FALAA TATANAAJAWA BIL-ISME WAL U’UDWAANE WAMAA’SEETE RASOOLE WATANAAJAWA BIL-BIRRE WAALTTAQWAA WAT TAQUL LAAHA LAZEE ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nO ye who believe! When ye hold secret counsel, do it not for iniquity and hostility, and disobedience to the Prophet; but do it for righteousness and self-restraint; and fear Allah, to Whom ye shall be brought back. \nاِنَّمَا النَّجْوٰى مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ لِيَحْزُنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَيْسَ بِضَآرِّهِمْ شَيْئًا اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(10)\nINNAMAA AN-NAJWAA MENAL SHAYTAANE LEEHZUNA LAZEENA AAMANOO BE-AN BEZAARREHEM SHAY-ANW ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\nSecret counsels are only (inspired) by the Evil One, in order that he may cause grief to the Believers; but he cannot harm them in the least, except as Allah permits; and on Allah let the Believers put their trust. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا قِيْلَ لَكُمْ تَفَسَّحُوْا فِى الْمَجٰلِسِ فَافْسَحُوْا يَفْسَحِ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ ۚ وَاِذَا قِيْلَ انْشُزُوْا فَانْشُزُوْا يَرْفَعِ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْكُمْ ۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ دَرَجٰتٍ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(11)\nYAA-AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA QEELA LAKUM TAFASSAHOOA FIL AL-MAJAALESE FAAFSAHOOA YAFSAHE LAAHO LAKUM WA EZAA QEELA ANSHUZOOA FAANSHUZOOA YARFAE’E LAAHO LAZEENA AAMANOO MINKUM WAL LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA DARAJAATIN WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nO ye who believe! When ye are told to make room in the assemblies, (spread out and) make room: (ample) room will Allah provide for you. And when ye are told to rise up, rise up Allah will rise up, to (suitable) ranks (and degrees), those of you who believe and who have been granted (mystic) Knowledge. And Allah is well-acquainted with all ye do. \nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا نَاجَيْتُمُ الرَّسُوْلَ فَقَدِّمُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ نَجْوٰٮكُمْ صَدَقَةً  ؕ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ وَاَطْهَرُ ؕ فَاِنْ لَّمْ تَجِدُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(12)\nYAA-AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA NAAJAYTUMU YATTABE-U’R FAQADDEMOOA BAYNA YADAY NAJWAAKUM SADAQATAN ZAA LEKA KHAYRUL LAKUM WA ATHARO FA-IN LAM WA LAM FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nO ye who believe! When ye consult the Messenger in private, spend something in charity before your private consultation. That will be best for you, and most conducive to purity (of conduct). But if ye find not (the wherewithal), Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful. \nءَاَشْفَقْتُمْ اَنْ تُقَدِّمُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ نَجْوٰٮكُمْ صَدَقٰتٍ ؕ فَاِذْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوْا وَتَابَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمْ فَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(13)\nAASHFAQTUM AN WA BAYNA YADAY NAJWAAKUM SADAQAATIN FA IZ LAM TAF-A’LOO WA TAABA LAAHO A’LAYKUM FAAQEEMOOA SALAATA WA AAATOOA ZAKAATA WAATEEU’OOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WAL LAAHO KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nIs it that ye are afraid of spending sums in charity before your private consultation (with him)? If, then, ye do not so, and Allah forgives you, then (at least) establish regular prayer; practise regular charity; and obey Allah and His Messenger. And Allah is well-acquainted with all that ye do. \nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ تَوَلَّوْا قَوْمًا غَضِبَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ مَّا هُمْ مِّنْكُمْ وَلَا مِنْهُمْۙ وَيَحْلِفُوْنَ عَلَى الْكَذِبِ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(14)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA TAWALLAW QAWMAN GHAZEBAL LAAHO A’ALAYHEM MAA HUM MINKUM WA LAA MINHUM WAYAHLEFOONA A’LAL AL-KAZEBE WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nTurnest thou not thy attention to those who turn (in friendship) to such as have the Wrath of Allah upon them? They are neither of you nor of them, and they swear to falsehood knowingly. \nاَعَدَّ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْ عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ سَآءَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(15)\nA-A’DDA LAAHO LAHUM A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAA INNAHUM SAAA-A MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAllah has prepared for them a severe Penalty: evil indeed are their deeds. \nاِتَّخَذُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ جُنَّةً فَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(16)\nITTAKHAZOO AYMAANAHUM JUNNATAN FA-SADDU A’N SABEELIL LAAHE FALAHUM A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nThey have made their oaths a screen (for their misdeeds): thus they obstruct (men) from the Path of Allah: therefore shall they have a humiliating Penalty. \nلَنْ تُغْنِىَ عَنْهُمْ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ ؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(17)\nLAN TUGHNEAAA A’NHUM AAMWAALUHUM WA LAA AAWLAADUHUM MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nOf no profit whatever to them, against Allah, will be their riches nor their sons: they will be Companions of the Fire, to dwell therein (for aye)! \nيَوْمَ يَبْعَثُهُمُ اللّٰهُ جَمِيْعًا فَيَحْلِفُوْنَ لَهٗ كَمَا يَحْلِفُوْنَ لَكُمْ وَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(18)\nYAWMA YABA’ASUHUMU LAAHO JAMEE-A’A FAYAHLEFOONA LAHU KAMAA YAHLEFOONA LAKUM WA YAHSABOONAL ANNAHUM A’LAA SHAY-IN ALAA INNAHUM HOMUL AL-KAAZEBOONA.\nOne day will Allah raise them all up (for Judgment): then will they swear to Him as they swear to you: And they think that they have something (to stand upon). No, indeed! they are but liars! \nاِسْتَحْوَذَ عَلَيْهِمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ فَاَنْسٰٮهُمْ ذِكْرَ اللّٰهِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ حِزْبُ الشَّيْطٰنِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ حِزْبَ الشَّيْطٰنِ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(19)\nAESTAHWAZA A’LAYHEMUL SHAYTAANO FA-ANSAAHUM ZEKRA LAAH OOLAAA-EKA HEZBU SHAYTAAN ALAA INNAL HEZBA SHAYTAANE HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nThe Evil One has got the better of them: so he has made them lose the remembrance of Allah. They are the Party of the Evil One. Truly, it is the Party of the Evil One that will perish! \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُحَآدُّوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ فِى الْاَذَلِّيْنَ‏(20)\nINNAL LAZEENA YUHAADDOONA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU OOLAAA-EKA FIL AL-AAZALLEENA.\nThose who resist Allah and His Messenger will be among those most humiliated. \nكَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَاَغْلِبَنَّ اَنَا وَرُسُلِىْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَوِىٌّ عَزِيْزٌ‏(21)\nKATABAL LAAHO LAAGHLEBANNA ANAA WARUSULEAA INNAL LAAHA QAWEAAAUN A’ZEEZUN.\nAllah has decreed: “It is I and My messengers who must prevail”: For Allah is One full of strength, able to enforce His Will. \nلَا تَجِدُ قَوْمًا يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ يُوَآدُّوْنَ مَنْ حَآدَّ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَلَوْ كَانُوْۤا اٰبَآءَهُمْ اَوْ اَبْنَآءَهُمْ اَوْ اِخْوَانَهُمْ اَوْ عَشِيْرَتَهُمْؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ كَتَبَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمُ الْاِيْمَانَ وَاَيَّدَهُمْ بِرُوْحٍ مِّنْهُ ؕ وَيُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ رَضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ حِزْبُ اللّٰهِ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ حِزْبَ اللّٰهِ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(22)\nLAA TAJEDU QAWMAN YOAMENOON BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE YOOAAADDOONA MAN HAADDA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA LAW KAANOO AA-BAAA-AHUM AW YOZABBEHO AW AEKHWAANAHUM AW A’ASHEERATAHUM OOLAAA-EKA KATABAL FEE QOLOOBEHEMUR EEMAANA WAAYYADAHUM BEROOHIN MINHO WAYUDKHELUHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA RAZEYAL LAAHO A’NHUM WARAZOOA A’NHO OOLAAA-EKA HEZBU LAAHE ALAA INNAL HEZBA LAAHE HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThou wilt not find any people who believe in Allah and the Last Day, loving those who resist Allah and His Messenger, even though they were their fathers or their sons, or their brothers, or their kindred. For such He has written Faith in their hearts, and strengthened them with a spirit from Himself. And He will admit them to Gardens beneath which Rivers flow, to dwell therein (for ever). Allah will be well pleased with them, and they with Him. They are the Party of Allah. Truly it is the Party of Allah that will achieve Felicity. ",
  "merits": "Surah Mujaadelah (The Pleading One)\nThere are 22 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Madinah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will be from among the thankful servants of Allah (s.w.t.) on the Day of Judgement. If Surah al-Mujaadelah is recited near a sick person, or worn by the sick person as a talisman, he will be cured of his illness. If recited on anything that has been buried in the ground, it will remain protected until the person himself removes it.\nReciting this Surah brings a feeling of ease to a restless person. Constant recitation also protects one from thieves. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that recitation of this Surah keeps one safe from the evil designs of Jinn and men. If recited on dust or sand and then thrown towards the enemy, he is easily overcome."
